[753.856,"o","ov stack destroy -y --delete-data\r\n"]
[753.893,"o","── PLAN · nothing below has run ───────────────────────────────────────\r\nThis is what will be deleted from your Google Cloud project ***:\r\n\r\n  # Everything the Terraform state in .openvidu/gcp holds: the four masters, the load\r\n  # balancer (its forwarding rules, backend and health check), the media nodes' instance\r\n  # group, its instance template and autoscaler, the scale-in function and its Cloud\r\n  # Scheduler job, their disks, the load balancer's static address, the firewall rules,\r\n  # the service accounts, the buckets' HMAC key, the secrets, the buckets with the\r\n  # recordings and Meet data and with the cluster's metrics and logs.\r\n  terraform -chdir=.openvidu/gcp init -input=false -no-color -force-copy\r\n  terraform -chdir=.openvidu/gcp destroy -auto-approve -input=false -no-color\r\n\r\n  # Media nodes the scale-in function abandoned from their group are not in the state;\r\n  # they are listed and deleted too.\r\n  gcloud compute instances list --project=*** '--filter=name~^openvidu-e2e-gcp-ha-a125636-media-node' '--format=value(name,zone.basename())'\r\n\r\n--delete-data: the recordings and Meet data, and the cluster's metrics and logs, are in the stack's two Cloud Storage buckets: this deletes them.\r\n── end of plan ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\r\n\r\n"]
[755.884,"o","\r\n▶ Delete the machines on Google Cloud…\r\n"]
[756.848,"o","   · destroy .openvidu/gcp (this returns when Terraform is done)\r\n"]
